          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figs. (i), (ii), and (iii) are quadrilaterals, and the others are not. Why?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.831,
            0.848,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The angles",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of a quadrilateral are the angles between its sides, as marked in Figs. (i), (ii), and (iii)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.867,
            0.848,
            0.907
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We will start with the most familiar quadrilaterals — rectangles and squares."
